window.SOURATE_DATA = {"numSourate":74,"nomSourate":"Al-Muddaththir","nomFr":"Celui qui se couvre","nomEn":"The Cloaked One","nomEs":"El Arropado","nomArabe":"المدثر","lieu":"La Mecque","typeSourateLabel":"Sourate Mecquoise","typeSourateClasse":"mecquoise","ordreRev":4,"nbVersets":56,"versets":[{"numVerset":1,"texteArabe":"يَٰٓأَيُّهَا الْمُدَّثِّرُ","tradPropre":"O, toi (Muhammad)! Le revêtu d'un manteau!","tradEn":"O you who covers himself [with a garment],","tradEs":"¡Oh, tú [Mujámmad] que te envuelves en un manto!","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Interpellation du Prophète ﷺ enveloppé dans son manteau.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Hadith de Jābir ibn ‘Abdillāh (Al-Bukhārī) :</strong> Le Prophète ﷺ raconta qu'à la fin de sa retraite à Hirā', en descendant de la montagne, il entendit une voix l'appeler. Regardant autour de lui sans rien voir, il leva les yeux au ciel et aperçut l'Ange Gabriel (Jibrīl) sous sa forme originelle. Saisi de frayeur, il rentra auprès de Khadījah en demandant qu'on le couvre d'un manteau et qu'on lui verse de l'eau froide ; Allāh fit alors descendre ce verset.","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Address to the Prophet ﷺ wrapped in his cloak.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Hadith of Jābir ibn ‘Abdillāh (Sahīh Al-Bukhārī):</strong> Returning from his retreat at Hirā', the Prophet ﷺ heard a voice, looked up, and saw Angel Gabriel (Jibrīl) in his original form between heaven and earth. Trembling, he returned to Khadījah asking to be covered with a cloak and poured over with cold water, whereupon Allāh revealed these verses.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Hadiz de Jābir ibn ‘Abdillāh (Sahīh Al-Bukhārī):</strong><br><br>Al descender de Hirā', el Profeta ﷺ vio al Ángel Gabriel en su forma original entre el cielo y la tierra; regresó temblando ante Khadījah pidiendo ser cubierto con un manto, y Allah reveló estos versículos.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الْمُدَّثِّرُ﴾</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>حديث جابر بن عبد الله رضي الله عنهما (صحيح البخاري) :</strong> أخبر النبي ﷺ أنه بعد جواره بحراء سمع نداءً فرفع رأسه فرأى جبريل عليه السلام على صورته التي خُلق عليها، فرجع إلى خديجة رضي الله عنها فقال: <em>«دثّروني وصبّوا عليّ ماءً باردًا»</em>، فأنزل الله هذه الآيات.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074001","lienPrecedent":"sourate-73-verset-20.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-2.html"},{"numVerset":2,"texteArabe":"قُمْ فَأَنذِرْ","tradPropre":"Lève-toi et avertis.","tradEn":"Arise and warn","tradEs":"Ponte de pie y advierte.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Ordre de se lever avec détermination pour avertir l'humanité.</strong><br><br>La mission prophétique passe ici à l'avertissement public afin de prévenir les hommes qu'ils rendront des comptes devant le Tout-Puissant.","explicationEn":"2. Arise and warn of Allah’s punishment.","explicationEs":"2. Levántate y advierte del castigo de Allah.","explicationAr":"انهض فخوِّف من عذاب الله.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074002","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-1.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-3.html"},{"numVerset":3,"texteArabe":"وَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْ","tradPropre":"Et de ton Seigneur, célèbre la grandeur.","tradEn":"And your Lord glorify","tradEs":"Proclama la grandeza de tu Señor,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Proclamer la grandeur suprême d'Allāh (Takbīr).</strong><br><br>Louer son Seigneur et célébrer Sa grandeur au-dessus de tout associé.","explicationEn":"3. Declare the greatness of your Lord.","explicationEs":"3. Declara la grandeza de tu Señor.","explicationAr":"وعَظِّمْ ربك.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074003","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-2.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-4.html"},{"numVerset":4,"texteArabe":"وَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرْ","tradPropre":"Et tes vêtements, purifie-les.","tradEn":"And your clothing purify","tradEs":"purifica tus vestimentas,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Injonction de purifier ses vêtements, son cœur et ses actes.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Synthèse des exégètes :</strong> Ibn ‘Abbās et Qatādah l'expliquent par la purification de l'âme et des œuvres ; Muhammad ibn Sīrīn et Ibn Zayd par le lavage physique des habits (contrairement aux polythéistes) ; et Sa‘īd ibn Jubayr par la pureté du cœur et de l'intention.","explicationEn":"4. Purify yourself from sins and your clothes from impurities.","explicationEs":"4. Purifícate de los pecados y a tus vestimentas de las impurezas.","explicationAr":"وطهِّر نفسك من الذنوب وثيابك من النجاسات.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074004","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-3.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-5.html"},{"numVerset":5,"texteArabe":"وَالرُّجْزَ فَاهْجُرْ","tradPropre":"Et de tout péché, écarte-toi.","tradEn":"And uncleanliness avoid","tradEs":"apártate de la idolatría,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Ordre de délaisser les idoles et toute désobéissance (Ar-Rujz), selon Ibn ‘Abbās et Ad-Dahhāk.</strong>","explicationEn":"5. Keep away from the worship of idols.","explicationEs":"5. Apártate de la adoración de los ídolos.","explicationAr":"وابتعد عن عبادة الأوثان.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074005","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-4.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-6.html"},{"numVerset":6,"texteArabe":"وَلَا تَمْنُن تَسْتَكْثِرُ","tradPropre":"Et ne donne pas dans le but de recevoir davantage.","tradEn":"And do not confer favor to acquire more","tradEs":"y no des esperando recibir más a cambio.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Ne pas donner dans l'espoir de recevoir davantage des hommes (avis d'Ibn ‘Abbās retenu par Ibn Kathīr), ni attendre de salaire terrestre pour la mission (selon Ibn Zayd).</strong>","explicationEn":"6. Do not think that you have done a favour to your Lord by regarding your righteous actions to be plenty.","explicationEs":"6. No pienses que le has hecho un favor a tu Señor al considerar que tus obras rectas son abundantes.","explicationAr":"ولا تمنن على ربك بأن تستكثر عملك الصالح.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074006","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-5.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-7.html"},{"numVerset":7,"texteArabe":"وَلِرَبِّكَ فَاصْبِرْ","tradPropre":"Et pour ton Seigneur, endure.","tradEn":"But for your Lord be patient.","tradEs":"Sé paciente [con las dificultades que enfrentarás al divulgar el Mensaje] de tu Señor.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Endurer avec patience pour la Face d'Allāh face aux épreuves de la mission.</strong>","explicationEn":"7. Be patient for Allah’s sake over the harm that you incur.","explicationEs":"7. Sé paciente por la causa de Allah ante las dificultades que enfrentarás.","explicationAr":"واصبر لله على ما تلاقيه من الأذى.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074007","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-6.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-8.html"},{"numVerset":8,"texteArabe":"فَإِذَا نُقِرَ فِي النَّاقُورِ","tradPropre":"Quand on sonnera du Clairon,","tradEn":"And when the trumpet is blown,","tradEs":"[Pero ten en cuenta que] cuando se sople la trompeta [y comience el Día del Juicio],","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Le souffle dans le Clairon (An-Nāqūr) annonçant le Jour du Jugement,</strong>","explicationEn":"8. When the trumpet will be blown a second time.","explicationEs":"8. Cuando suene la trompeta por segunda vez.","explicationAr":"فإذا نُفِخَ في القرن النفخة الثانية.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074008","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-7.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-9.html"},{"numVerset":9,"texteArabe":"فَذَٰلِكَ يَوْمَئِذٖ يَوْمٌ عَسِيرٌ","tradPropre":"alors, ce jour-là sera un jour difficile,","tradEn":"That Day will be a difficult day","tradEs":"ese será un día difícil.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>un Jour redoutable et éprouvant,</strong>","explicationEn":"9. That day will be a severe day.","explicationEs":"9. Ese día será un día difícil.","explicationAr":"فذلك اليوم يوم شديد.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074009","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-8.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-10.html"},{"numVerset":10,"texteArabe":"عَلَى الْكَٰفِرِينَ غَيْرُ يَسِيرٖ","tradPropre":"pas facile pour les mécréants.","tradEn":"For the disbelievers - not easy.","tradEs":"Nada fácil para los que hoy desmienten la verdad.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>dépourvu de toute facilité pour ceux qui ont rejeté la foi.</strong>","explicationEn":"10. For those who reject Allah and His messengers it will not be easy.","explicationEs":"10. Para aquellos que rechazan a Allah y a Sus Mensajeros no será nada fácil.","explicationAr":"على الكافرين بالله وبرسله غير سهل.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074010","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-9.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-11.html"},{"numVerset":11,"texteArabe":"ذَرْنِي وَمَنْ خَلَقْتُ وَحِيدٗا","tradPropre":"Laisse-Moi avec celui que J'ai créé seul,","tradEn":"Leave Me with the one I created alone","tradEs":"[Oh, Mujámmad] Deja que Yo me encargaré de aquel que he creado, y vino al mundo solo,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Avertissement visant Al-Walīd ibn Al-Mughīrah (des Banū Makhzūm) :</strong><br><br>Créé seul sans fortune ni enfants à sa naissance, comblé ensuite de richesses étendues (v.12) et de fils restant constamment auprès de lui à La Mecque sans avoir besoin de voyager pour commercer (v.13), il s'obstina pourtant à renier le Coran (v.16).","explicationEn":"11. Leave me, O Messenger, and the one whom I created alone in the womb of his mother without wealth or children (This refers to Walid bin Al Mughira).","explicationEs":"11.¡Mensajero!, deja que Allah se encargue de aquel que creó solo en el vientre de su madre sin riquezas ni hijos (Al-Walíd Ibn Al-Mughira).","explicationAr":"اتركني - أيها الرسول - ومن خلقته وحيدًا في بطن أمه دون مال أو ولد (وهو الوليد بن المُغِيرة).","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074011","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-10.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-12.html"},{"numVerset":12,"texteArabe":"وَجَعَلْتُ لَهُ مَالٗا مَّمْدُودٗا","tradPropre":"et à qui J'ai donné des biens étendus,","tradEn":"And to whom I granted extensive wealth","tradEs":"a quien concedí abundantes riquezas","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>avant de lui octroyer une fortune étendue issue de son grand commerce,</strong>","explicationEn":"12. I gave him plenty wealth.","explicationEs":"12. Él le concedió abundante riqueza.","explicationAr":"وجعلت له مالًا كثيرًا.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074012","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-11.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-13.html"},{"numVerset":13,"texteArabe":"وَبَنِينَ شُهُودٗا","tradPropre":"et des enfants qui lui tiennent toujours compagnie,","tradEn":"And children present [with him]","tradEs":"y numerosos hijos atentos.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>et de nombreux fils demeurant toujours à ses côtés à La Mecque sans avoir besoin de voyager,</strong>","explicationEn":"13. I gave him children who were present with him, who attended gatherings with him and who did not leave him on account of travel due to the abundance of his wealth.","explicationEs":"13. Le concedió hijos que estaban con él, que asistieron a reuniones con él y que no lo abandonaron, debido a la abundancia de su riqueza.","explicationAr":"وجعلت له بنين حاضرين معه ويشهدون المحافل معه لا يفارقونه لسفر لكثرة ماله.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074013","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-12.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-14.html"},{"numVerset":14,"texteArabe":"وَمَهَّدتُّ لَهُ تَمْهِيدٗا","tradPropre":"pour qui aussi J'ai aplani toutes difficultés","tradEn":"And spread [everything] before him, easing [his life].","tradEs":"Y le facilité medios con holgura,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>tout en lui aplanissant toutes les facilités matérielles de ce bas monde.</strong>","explicationEn":"14. I extended to him his livelihood, provision and children profusely.","explicationEs":"14. Allah le facilitó su sustento, provisión e hijos con holgura.","explicationAr":"وبسطت له في العيش والرزق والولد بسطًا.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074014","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-13.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-15.html"},{"numVerset":15,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ يَطْمَعُ أَنْ أَزِيدَ","tradPropre":"Cependant, il convoite [de Moi] que Je lui donne davantage.","tradEn":"Then he desires that I should add more.","tradEs":"pero aun así anhela más.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Malgré cela, il convoite avec arrogance davantage de faveurs sans croire,</strong>","explicationEn":"15. Then despite his denial of Me he desires that I give him more after I gave him all of that.","explicationEs":"15. Pero a pesar de negar a Allah, desea que Él le dé más, después de haberle dado todo.","explicationAr":"ثم يطمع مع كفره بي أن أزيده بعد ما أعطيته من ذلك كله.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074015","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-14.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-16.html"},{"numVerset":16,"texteArabe":"كَلَّآ إِنَّهُ كَانَ لِأٓيَٰتِنَا عَنِيدٗا","tradPropre":"Pas du tout! Car il reniait nos versets (le Coran) avec entêtement.","tradEn":"No! Indeed, he has been toward Our verses obstinate.","tradEs":"¡No! Porque rechazó Mis signos.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>car il s'obstine à renier le Coran et à combattre le Messager d'Allāh ﷺ.</strong>","explicationEn":"16. The matter is not as he thinks. He was opposed to My verses that I revealed to My messenger denying them.","explicationEs":"16. Pero no es como él piensa, porque rechazó las aleyas que Él le revelé a Su mensajero.","explicationAr":"ليس الأمر كما تصوّر، إنه كان معاندًا لآياتنا المنزلة على رسولنا مكذبًا بها.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074016","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-15.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-17.html"},{"numVerset":17,"texteArabe":"سَأُرْهِقُهُ صَعُودًا","tradPropre":"Je vais le contraindre à gravir une pente.","tradEn":"I will cover him with arduous torment.","tradEs":"Haré que sus dificultades vayan en aumento.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Le supplice de la montagne « Sa‘ūd ».</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Hadith d'Abū Sa‘īd Al-Khudrī :</strong> Le Prophète ﷺ a indiqué que <em>Sa‘ūd</em> est une montagne de feu en Enfer que le damné sera forcé de gravir sans répit : dès qu'il y posera la main, elle fondra, puis reprendra sa forme lorsqu'il la relèvera.","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>The torment of Mount Sa‘ūd.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Hadith of Abū Sa‘īd Al-Khudrī:</strong> The Prophet ﷺ explained that <em>Sa‘ūd</em> is a fiery mountain in Hell which the disbeliever (Al-Walīd ibn Al-Mughīrah) will be forced to climb perpetually.","explicationEs":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Hadiz de Abū Sa‘īd Al-Khudrī:</strong><br><br><em>Sa‘ūd</em> es una montaña de fuego en el Infierno que Al-Walīd ibn Al-Mughīrah será forzado a escalar sin descanso.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿سَأُرْهِقُهُ صَعُودًا﴾</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>حديث أبي سعيد الخدري :</strong> «صعود» جبل من نار في جهنم يُكلّف الوليد بن المغيرة صعوده أبدًا، كلما وضع يده عليه ذابت فإذا رفعها عادت.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074017","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-16.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-18.html"},{"numVerset":18,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهُ فَكَّرَ وَقَدَّرَ","tradPropre":"Il a réfléchi. Et il a décidé.","tradEn":"Indeed, he thought and deliberated.","tradEs":"Porque él pensó y decidió [a sabiendas, desmentir el Mensaje].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>La délibération d'Al-Walīd contre le Coran.</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Récit d'As-Suddī :</strong> Lorsque les Qurayshites se concertèrent pour qualifier le Prophète ﷺ de poète, de devin, de magicien ou de possédé (voir aussi Sourate 17:48), Al-Walīd réfléchit, fronça les sourcils d'un air grave (v.21-22), se détourna avec orgueil (v.23) et déclara que le Coran n'était qu'une magie apprise et une parole humaine (v.24-25).","explicationEn":"18. This disbeliever whom I bestowed with those favours thought about what he should say in order to refute the Qur’ān, and planned this within himself.","explicationEs":"18. Este incrédulo, a quien Allah le concedió esos favores, pensó en lo que debía decir para desmentir el Corán, y planeó esto dentro de sí mismo.","explicationAr":"إن هذا الكافر الذي أنعمت عليه بتلك النعم فكّر فيما يقوله في القرآن لإبطاله، وقدّر ذلك في نفسه.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074018","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-17.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-19.html"},{"numVerset":19,"texteArabe":"فَقُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَ","tradPropre":"Qu'il périsse! Comme il a décidé!","tradEn":"So may he be destroyed [for] how he deliberated.","tradEs":"Fue maldecido por la decisión que tomó.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>malédiction divine contre cette décision funeste et calomnieuse,</strong>","explicationEn":"19. So may he be cursed and punished. How did he plan!","explicationEs":"19. Entonces, que sea maldecido y castigado. ¡Por sus planes malvados!","explicationAr":"فلُعِن وعُذِّب كيف قَدَّر.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074019","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-18.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-20.html"},{"numVerset":20,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ قُتِلَ كَيْفَ قَدَّرَ","tradPropre":"Encore une fois, qu'il périsse; comme il a décidé!","tradEn":"Then may he be destroyed [for] how he deliberated.","tradEs":"¡Sí!, fue maldecido por la decisión que tomó.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>répétition solennelle soulignant la gravité de son mensonge délibéré,</strong>","explicationEn":"20. Again, may he be cursed and punished. How did he plan!","explicationEs":"20. Una vez más, que sea maldecido y castigado. ¡Por sus planes malvados!","explicationAr":"ثم لعن وعذّب كيف قَدَّر.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074020","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-19.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-21.html"},{"numVerset":21,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ نَظَرَ","tradPropre":"Ensuite, il a regardé.","tradEn":"Then he considered [again];","tradEs":"Luego meditó [cómo desacreditar la revelación],","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>il observa son assemblée après avoir réfléchi,</strong>","explicationEn":"21. Then he reconsidered and carefully thought about what he should say.","explicationEs":"21. Luego reconsideró y pensó cuidadosamente sobre lo que debería decir.","explicationAr":"ثم أعاد النظر والتروِّي فيما يقول.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074021","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-20.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-22.html"},{"numVerset":22,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ عَبَسَ وَبَسَرَ","tradPropre":"Et il s'est renfrogné et a durci son visage.","tradEn":"Then he frowned and scowled;","tradEs":"pero [al no poder encontrar ningún argumento] frunció el ceño y ofuscó el semblante.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>fronça les sourcils et durcit son visage devant la vérité,</strong>","explicationEn":"22. The he frowned and scowled when he did not find anything to challenge the Qur’ān with.","explicationEs":"22. Frunció el ceño y ofuscó el semblante cuando no encontró nada con qué desafiar al Corán.","explicationAr":"ثم قَطَّب وجهه وكَلَح حين لم يجد ما يطعن به في القرآن.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074022","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-21.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-23.html"},{"numVerset":23,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ أَدْبَرَ وَاسْتَكْبَرَ","tradPropre":"Ensuite il a tourné le dos et s'est enflé d'orgueil","tradEn":"Then he turned back and was arrogant","tradEs":"Luego le dio la espalda [al Mensaje] y se comportó con soberbia,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>puis détourna le dos en s'enflant d'orgueil,</strong>","explicationEn":"23. Then he turned away from faith and was too proud to follow the Prophet (peace be upon him).","explicationEs":"23. Luego se apartó de la fe y fue demasiado soberbio para seguir al Profeta r.","explicationAr":"ثم أدبر عن الإيمان، واستكبر عن اتباع النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074023","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-22.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-24.html"},{"numVerset":24,"texteArabe":"فَقَالَ إِنْ هَٰذَآ إِلَّا سِحْرٞ يُؤْثَرُ","tradPropre":"Puis il a dit: «Ceci (le Coran) n'est que magie apprise","tradEn":"And said, \"This is not but magic imitated [from others].","tradEs":"diciendo: \"Esto solo es hechicería que impresiona.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>en prétendant que le Coran n'est qu'une magie transmise,</strong>","explicationEn":"24. He said: This what Muhammad brought is not Allah’s speech, but it is sorcery that he relates from others.","explicationEs":"24. Dijo: “Esto que recita Mujámmad no es la palabra de Allah, sino una hechicería que impresiona a las personas.","explicationAr":"فقال: ليس هذا الذي جاء به محمد كلام الله، بل هو سحر يرويه عن غيره.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074024","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-23.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-25.html"},{"numVerset":25,"texteArabe":"إِنْ هَٰذَآ إِلَّا قَوْلُ الْبَشَرِ","tradPropre":"ce n'est là que la parole d'un humain».","tradEn":"This is not but the word of a human being.\"","tradEs":"Es la palabra de un mortal\".","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>et une simple parole humaine !</strong>","explicationEn":"25. This is not Allah’s speech, but it is the speech of man.","explicationEs":"25. Esta no es la palabra de Allah, sino la palabra de un hombre”.","explicationAr":"ليس هذا كلام الله، بل هو كلام الإنس.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074025","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-24.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-26.html"},{"numVerset":26,"texteArabe":"سَأُصْلِيهِ سَقَرَ","tradPropre":"Je vais le brûler dans le Feu intense (Saqar).","tradEn":"I will drive him into Saqar.","tradEs":"En consecuencia, lo llevaré al fuego del Infierno.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Condamnation au brasier intense de « Saqar »,</strong>","explicationEn":"26. I will enter this disbeliever into one of the levels of the Fire, which is Saqar, to suffer from its heat.","explicationEs":"26. Llevaré a este incrédulo a uno de los niveles del Fuego, que es As-Saqar, para que sufra su calor.","explicationAr":"سأدخل هذا الكافر طبقة من طبقات النار، وهي سَقَر يقاسي حرّها.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074026","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-25.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-27.html"},{"numVerset":27,"texteArabe":"وَمَآ أَدْرَىٰكَ مَا سَقَرُ","tradPropre":"Et qui te dira ce qu'est Saqar?","tradEn":"And what can make you know what is Saqar?","tradEs":"¿Y qué te hará comprender lo que es el fuego del Infierno?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>interrogation soulignant l'horreur indescriptible de cette fournaise,</strong>","explicationEn":"27. What will tell you, O Muhammad, what Saqar is?!","explicationEs":"27. ¿Qué te hará comprender, Mujámmad, lo que es el As-Saqar?","explicationAr":"وما أعلمك - يا محمد - ما سَقَر؟!","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074027","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-26.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-28.html"},{"numVerset":28,"texteArabe":"لَا تُبْقِي وَلَا تَذَرُ","tradPropre":"Il ne laisse rien et n'épargne rien;","tradEn":"It lets nothing remain and leaves nothing [unburned],","tradEs":"[Es un fuego que] no deja nada sin quemar ni cesa jamás.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>qui dévore et détruit tout sans rien épargner,</strong>","explicationEn":"28. It does not spare any person that is punished in it except that it comes on him and does not leave him. Then he returns to how it was and it comes to him, again and again.","explicationEs":"28. Es un fuego que lo consume todo y repite su castigo una y otra vez.","explicationAr":"لا تُبْقِي شيئًا من المُعَذَّب فيها إلا أتت عليه، ولا تتركه، ثم يعود كما كان، ثم تأتي عليه، وهكذا دَوَالَيْك.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074028","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-27.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-29.html"},{"numVerset":29,"texteArabe":"لَوَّاحَةٞ لِّلْبَشَرِ","tradPropre":"Il brûle la peau et la noircit.","tradEn":"Blackening the skins.","tradEs":"Abrasa la piel.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>calcinant et noircissant les peaux.</strong>","explicationEn":"29. It severely burns and alters skins.","explicationEs":"29. Abrasa y quema severamente la piel.","explicationAr":"شديدة الإحراق والتغيير للجلود.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074029","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-28.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-30.html"},{"numVerset":30,"texteArabe":"عَلَيْهَا تِسْعَةَ عَشَرَ","tradPropre":"Ils sont dix neuf à y veiller.","tradEn":"Over it are nineteen [angels].","tradEs":"Hay diecinueve [ángeles] que lo custodian.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Les dix-neuf Anges gardiens de l'Enfer (Saqar).</strong><br><br>📜 <strong>Récit d'Ibn Abī Hātim :</strong> Lorsque des juifs interrogèrent un compagnon sur le nombre des gardiens de l'Enfer, Allāh révéla qu'ils sont dix-neuf Anges rudes et puissants (Sourate 66:6). Le verset 31 précise que ce nombre sert d'épreuve pour les négateurs, de preuve convaincante pour les Gens du Livre (Torah et Évangile) et de renforcement pour la foi des croyants.","explicationEn":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Nineteen angelic guardians over Hellfire (Ibn Abī Hātim):</strong><br><br>Revealed as a trial for disbelievers, a confirmation for the People of the Book, and an increase in faith for the believers (v.31).","explicationEs":"30. Sus guardianes son diecinueve ángeles.","explicationAr":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>﴿عَلَيْهَا تِسْعَةَ عَشَرَ﴾</strong><br><br>📜 خزنة جهنم تسعة عشر من الملائكة الغلاظ الشداد (التحريم: 6)، جعل الله عدّتهم فتنةً للكافرين، ويقينًا لأهل الكتاب لموافقته ما عندهم، وزيادة إيمان للمؤمنين (آية 31).","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074030","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-29.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-31.html"},{"numVerset":31,"texteArabe":"وَمَا جَعَلْنَآ أَصْحَٰبَ النَّارِ إِلَّا مَلَٰٓئِكَةٗ وَمَا جَعَلْنَا عِدَّتَهُمْ إِلَّا فِتْنَةٗ لِّلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لِيَسْتَيْقِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ الْكِتَٰبَ وَيَزْدَادَ الَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِيمَٰنٗا وَلَا يَرْتَابَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ الْكِتَٰبَ وَالْمُؤْمِنُونَ وَلِيَقُولَ الَّذِينَ فِي قُلُوبِهِم مَّرَضٞ وَالْكَٰفِرُونَ مَاذَآ أَرَادَ اللَّهُ بِهَٰذَا مَثَلٗا كَذَٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ اللَّهُ مَن يَشَآءُ وَيَهْدِي مَن يَشَآءُ وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُودَ رَبِّكَ إِلَّا هُوَ وَمَا هِيَ إِلَّا ذِكْرَىٰ لِلْبَشَرِ","tradPropre":"Nous n'avons assigné comme gardiens du Feu que des Anges. Cependant, Nous n'en avons fixé le nombre que pour éprouver les mécréants, et aussi afin que ceux à qui le Livre a été apporté soient convaincus, et que croisse la foi de ceux qui croient, et que ceux à qui le Livre a été apporté et les croyants n'aient point de doute; et pour que ceux qui ont au cœur quelque maladie ainsi que les mécréants disent: «Qu'a donc voulu Allah par cette parabole?» C'est ainsi qu'Allah égare qui Il veut et guide qui Il veut. Nul ne connaît les armées de ton Seigneur, à part Lui. Et ce n'est là qu'un rappel pour les humains.","tradEn":"And We have not made the keepers of the Fire except angels. And We have not made their number except as a trial for those who disbelieve - that those who were given the Scripture will be convinced and those who have believed will increase in faith and those who were given the Scripture and the believers will not doubt and that those in whose hearts is hypocrisy and the disbelievers will say, \"What does Allah intend by this as an example?\" Thus does Allah leave astray whom He wills and guides whom He wills. And none knows the soldiers of your Lord except Him. And mention of the Fire is not but a reminder to humanity.","tradEs":"Decreté que los guardianes del Infierno fueran ángeles, y dispuse ese número para probar a los que rechazan la verdad, también para que la Gente del Libro se convenzan y crean, y para que los creyentes fortifiquen su fe y no les queden dudas a ellos ni a la Gente del Libro. También para que aquellos cuyos corazones están enfermos [de duda e hipocresía] y los que niegan la fe se pregunten: \"¿Qué es lo que quiere demostrar Dios con este ejemplo?\" Así es como Dios extravía a quien quiere [extraviarse] y guía a quien quiere [guiarse]. Solo Él conoce a todos los que sirven Su causa. Todo esto es motivo de reflexión para la humanidad.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>La sagesse du nombre dix-neuf :</strong><br><br>Fixé pour éprouver les mécréants (lorsqu'ils prétendirent pouvoir les vaincre), convaincre les Gens du Livre de la véracité du Prophète ﷺ par la concordance avec leurs Écritures anciennes, et renforcer la foi des croyants. Et nul ne connaît les armées de ton Seigneur à part Lui.","explicationEn":"31. I did not make the wardens of the Fire except angels, so humans do not have the power to face them. Abu Jahl was lying when he and his people claimed that they have the ability to attack them and then they will come out of the Fire. I did not make this number of theirs except to test those who reject Allah, so that the Jews who were given the Torah and the Christians who were given the Gospel will become certain when the Qur’ān that confirms what is in their scriptures is revealed, so that the faith of the believers increases when the people of the scripture agree with them and the Jews, Christians and the believers do not have any doubt, and so that those who waver in faith and those who are disbelievers say: What does Allah intend by this strange number?! Just as those who deny this number are misguided and those who accept it are guided, Allah misguides whoever He wishes to misguide and He guides whoever He wishes to guide. No one knows the forces of your Lord, because of their huge number, besides Him, may He be glorified. So let Abu Jahl who, mockingly and dismissively, said, “Does Muhammad only have nineteen aides?!” know this. The Fire is only a reminder for human beings, through which they can come to know of Allah’s greatness, may He be glorified.","explicationEs":"31. Hice que los guardianes del Fuego sean solo ángeles, por lo que los seres humanos no tienen el poder para enfrentarlos. Abu Yahl mentía cuando él y su gente afirmaron que tenían la capacidad de atacarlos y luego saldrían del Fuego. Dispuse este número de ángeles para probar a los que rechazan a Allah. Para que los judíos a quienes se les concedió la Torá y los cristianos a los que se les dio el Evangelio se convenzan cuando se revele el Corán, que confirma lo que está en sus escrituras, a fin de que la fe de los creyentes se incremente cuando la gente del Libro les confirme que eso está en sus escrituras, y los judíos, los cristianos y los creyentes no tengan duda alguna de su veracidad, y para que los que dudan en la fe y los incrédulos digan: “¿Qué pretende Allah con este extraño número?” De la misma manera que aquellos que niegan este número están en el error y aquellos que lo aceptan están en la guía, Allah extravía a quien quiere el extravío y guía a quien quiere guiarse. Nadie conoce el ejército de tu Señor, debido a su gran número, además de Él, glorificado sea. Entonces, deja que Abu Yahl, quien burlándose y con desdén dijo: “¿Mujámmad solo tiene diecinueve protectores?”, lo sepa. La advertencia del Fuego es solo un recordatorio.","explicationAr":"وما جعلنا خَزَنة النار إلا ملائكة، فلا طاقة للبشر بهم، وما جعلنا عددهم هذا إلا اختبارًا للذين كفروا بالله؛ ليقولوا ما قالوا فيُضاعَف عليهم العذاب، وليتيقّن اليهود الذين أعطوا التوراة، والنصارى الذين أعطوا الإنجيل حين نزل القرآن مصدقًا لما في كتابيهم، وليزداد المؤمنون إيمانًا عندما يوافقهم أهل الكتاب، ولا يرتاب اليهود والنصارى والمؤمنون، وليقول المترددون في الإيمان، والكافرون: أي شيء أراده الله بهذا العدد الغريب؟! مثل إضلال مُنْكِر هذا العدد وهداية المُصَدِّق به، يُضِلُّ الله من شاء أن يضلّه ويهدي من شاء أن يهديه، وما يعلم جنود ربك من كثرتها إلا هو سبحانه، وما النار إلا تذكرة للبشر يعلمون بها عظمة الله سبحانه.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074031","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-30.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-32.html"},{"numVerset":32,"texteArabe":"كَلَّا وَالْقَمَرِ","tradPropre":"Non!... Par la lune!","tradEn":"No! By the moon","tradEs":"[No es como pretenden los que rechazan la revelación, lo] juro por la Luna,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style=\"color:#ffffff;\">Il n’arrivera pas, comme le prétend un certain polythéiste, que ses compagnons viendront à bout des gardiens de l’Enfer et qu’ils finiront par en sortir.</strong> Allah prête ici serment par la lune.","explicationEn":"32. The statement is not as claimed by some idolaters that he will suffice his companions against the wardens of Hell and take them out of it. Allah took an oath by the moon.","explicationEs":"32. La realidad no es como afirman los idólatras, de que junto a sus compañeros podrán derrotar a los guardianes del Infierno y salir de allí. Allah lo jura por la Luna.","explicationAr":"ليس القول كما يزعم بعض المشركين أنه يكفي أصحابه خَزَنة جهنم حتى يُجْهِضهم عنها، أقسم الله بالقمر.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074032","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-31.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-33.html"},{"numVerset":33,"texteArabe":"وَالَّيْلِ إِذْ أَدْبَرَ","tradPropre":"Et par la nuit quand elle se retire!","tradEn":"And [by] the night when it departs","tradEs":"por la noche cuando desaparece,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis il prête serment par la nuit qui se termine","explicationEn":"33. He took an oath by the night when it departs.","explicationEs":"33. Allah hace un juramento por la noche cuando desaparece.","explicationAr":"وأقسم بالليل حين ولّى.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074033","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-32.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-34.html"},{"numVerset":34,"texteArabe":"وَالصُّبْحِ إِذَآ أَسْفَرَ","tradPropre":"Et par l'aurore quand elle se découvre!","tradEn":"And [by] the morning when it brightens,","tradEs":"por la mañana cuando resplandece,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"et par l’aube qui apparaît.","explicationEn":"34. He took an oath by the morning when it lights up.","explicationEs":"34. También jura por la mañana cuando se ilumina.","explicationAr":"وأقسم بالصبح إذا أضاء.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074034","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-33.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-35.html"},{"numVerset":35,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهَا لَإِحْدَى الْكُبَرِ","tradPropre":"[Saqar] est l'un des plus grands [malheurs]","tradEn":"Indeed, the Fire is of the greatest [afflictions]","tradEs":"que [el Infierno] es uno de los mayores [avisos],","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le Feu de l’Enfer est un des plus grands malheurs","explicationEn":"35. The fire of Hell is one the great calamities.","explicationEs":"35. Él jura que el fuego del Infierno es una de las grandes calamidades.","explicationAr":"إنّ نار جهنم لإحدى البلايا العظيمة.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074035","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-34.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-36.html"},{"numVerset":36,"texteArabe":"نَذِيرٗا لِّلْبَشَرِ","tradPropre":"un avertissement, pour les humains.","tradEn":"As a warning to humanity -","tradEs":"una advertencia para los seres humanos.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"et un avertissement qui menace et effraie les humains.","explicationEn":"36. In order to strike terror and fear in people.","explicationEs":"36. Para advertir a los seres humanos.","explicationAr":"ترهيبًا وتخويفًا للناس.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074036","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-35.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-37.html"},{"numVerset":37,"texteArabe":"لِمَن شَآءَ مِنكُمْ أَن يَتَقَدَّمَ أَوْ يَتَأَخَّرَ","tradPropre":"Pour qui d'entre vous, veut avancer ou reculer.","tradEn":"To whoever wills among you to proceed or stay behind.","tradEs":"Para que cada uno elija [libremente] obrar bien u obrar mal.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pour qui d’entre vous, ô gens, désire avancer dans la foi et les bonnes œuvres ou bien reculer dans la mécréance et les péchés.","explicationEn":"37. Whoever from amongst you, O people, wishes to go forward with faith in Allah and righteous actions, or to lag behind by disbelief and sins.","explicationEs":"37. Para quien desee tener fe en Allah y realizar obras justas, o desee mantenerse en la incredulidad y cometer pecados.","explicationAr":"لمن شاء منكم - أيها الناس - أن يتقدم بالإيمان بالله والعمل الصالح، أو يتأخر بالكفر والمعاصي.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074037","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-36.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-38.html"},{"numVerset":38,"texteArabe":"كُلُّ نَفْسِ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ رَهِينَةٌ","tradPropre":"Toute âme est l'otage de ce qu'elle a acquis.","tradEn":"Every soul, for what it has earned, will be retained","tradEs":"Toda alma será rehén de lo que haya hecho,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Toute âme demeure responsable et otage de ses propres actes,</strong>","explicationEn":"38. Every soul will be taken to task for the actions that it did. Either its actions will destroy it or they will release and rescue it from destruction.","explicationEs":"38. Cada alma será rehén de las acciones que cometió. Sus acciones lo destruirán o lo liberarán de la destrucción.","explicationAr":"كل نفس بما كسبته من الأعمال مأخوذة، فإما أن توبقها أعمالها، وإما أن تخلِّصها وتنقذها من الهلاك.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074038","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-37.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-39.html"},{"numVerset":39,"texteArabe":"إِلَّآ أَصْحَٰبَ الْيَمِينِ","tradPropre":"Sauf les gens de la droite (les élus):","tradEn":"Except the companions of the right,","tradEs":"salvo los [bienaventurados] de la derecha.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>hormis les Gens de la Droite (les élus sauvés par leur foi),</strong>","explicationEn":"39. Except for the believers, who wont be taken to task for their sins. Instead, these will be overlooked because of their righteous actions.","explicationEs":"39. Salvo los creyentes, que no serán rehenes de sus pecados, estos serán perdonados debido a sus acciones correctas.","explicationAr":"إلا المؤمنين فإنهم لا يُؤْخذون بذنوبهم، بل يتجاوز عنها لما لهم من عمل صالح.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074039","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-38.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-40.html"},{"numVerset":40,"texteArabe":"فِي جَنَّٰتٖ يَتَسَآءَلُونَ","tradPropre":"dans des Jardins, ils s'interrogeront","tradEn":"[Who will be] in gardens, questioning each other","tradEs":"[Ellos estarán] en jardines y se preguntarán unos a otros","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le Jour de la Résurrection, ils seront dans des Jardins où ils se questionneront les uns les autres","explicationEn":"40. On the Day of Judgement, they will be in gardens asking one another.","explicationEs":"40. En el Día del Juicio, estarán en jardines preguntándose unos a otros.","explicationAr":"وهم يوم القيامة في جنات يسأل بعضهم بعضًا.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074040","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-39.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-41.html"},{"numVerset":41,"texteArabe":"عَنِ الْمُجْرِمِينَ","tradPropre":"au sujet des criminels:","tradEn":"About the criminals,","tradEs":"acerca de [la situación] de los criminales.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"au sujet des criminels qui se sont conduits eux-mêmes en péchant, à la perdition.","explicationEn":"41. About the disbelievers who destroyed themselves by the sins they committed.","explicationEs":"41. Sobre los incrédulos que se destruyeron a sí mismos con los pecados que cometieron.","explicationAr":"عن الكافرين الذين أهلكوا أنفسهم بما عملوا من المعاصي.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074041","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-40.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-42.html"},{"numVerset":42,"texteArabe":"مَا سَلَكَكُمْ فِي سَقَرَ","tradPropre":"«Qu'est-ce qui vous a acheminés à Saqar?»","tradEn":"[And asking them], \"What put you into Saqar?\"","tradEs":"Y les preguntarán: \"¿Qué fue lo que los llevó al fuego del Infierno?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>qui interrogeront les criminels depuis le Paradis sur ce qui les a conduits dans « Saqar » :</strong>","explicationEn":"42. They will say to them: What entered you into Hell?","explicationEs":"42. Les dirán: “¿Qué les hizo ingresar al Infierno?”","explicationAr":"يقولون لهم: ما أدخلكم في جهنم؟","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074042","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-41.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-43.html"},{"numVerset":43,"texteArabe":"قَالُواْ لَمْ نَكُ مِنَ الْمُصَلِّينَ","tradPropre":"Ils diront: «Nous n'étions pas de ceux qui faisaient la Salât,","tradEn":"They will say, \"We were not of those who prayed,","tradEs":"Ellos responderán: \"Fue que no cumplíamos con la oración,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>les damnés avoueront qu'ils n'accomplissaient pas la prière obligatoire,</strong>","explicationEn":"43. The disbelievers will answer them saying: We were not of those who discharged the obligatory prayer in the worldly life.","explicationEs":"43. Los incrédulos les contestarán diciendo: “Éramos aquellos que no cumplían con la oración prescrita durante nuestra vida.","explicationAr":"فيجيبهم الكفار قائلين: لم نكن من الذين يؤدون الصلاة الواجبة في الحياة الدنيا.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074043","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-42.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-44.html"},{"numVerset":44,"texteArabe":"وَلَمْ نَكُ نُطْعِمُ الْمِسْكِينَ","tradPropre":"et nous ne nourrissions pas le pauvre,","tradEn":"Nor did we used to feed the poor.","tradEs":"no dábamos de comer al pobre,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>qu'ils refusaient de nourrir les pauvres et les nécessiteux,</strong>","explicationEn":"44. We did not feed the poor from what Allah gave us.","explicationEs":"44. No dábamos de comer a los pobres de lo que Allah nos dio.","explicationAr":"ولم نكن نطعم الفقير مما أعطانا الله.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074044","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-43.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-45.html"},{"numVerset":45,"texteArabe":"وَكُنَّا نَخُوضُ مَعَ الْخَآئِضِينَ","tradPropre":"et nous nous associions à ceux qui tenaient des conversations futiles,","tradEn":"And we used to enter into vain discourse with those who engaged [in it],","tradEs":"nos entreteníamos difamando [la revelación] junto a quienes retuercen la lógica para negar la verdad,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>qu'ils se mêlaient aux conversations vaines et moqueuses contre la Révélation,</strong>","explicationEn":"45. We used to be with the people of falsehood and go wherever they go. We used to speak to the people of misguidance and deviation.","explicationEs":"45. Solíamos juntarnos con las personas que difamaban la revelación para negarla y desviar a otros de la verdad.","explicationAr":"وكنا مع أهل الباطل ندور معهم أينما داروا، ونتحدث مع أهل الضلال والغواية.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074045","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-44.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-46.html"},{"numVerset":46,"texteArabe":"وَكُنَّا نُكَذِّبُ بِيَوْمِ الدِّينِ","tradPropre":"et nous traitions de mensonge le jour de la Rétribution,","tradEn":"And we used to deny the Day of Recompense","tradEs":"y desmentíamos la existencia del Día del Juicio","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>et qu'ils démentaient le Jour du Jugement,</strong>","explicationEn":"46. We used to deny the day of recompense.","explicationEs":"46. Solíamos desmentir el día del Juicio y la retribución.","explicationAr":"وكنا نكذب بيوم الجزاء.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074046","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-45.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-47.html"},{"numVerset":47,"texteArabe":"حَتَّىٰٓ أَتَىٰنَا الْيَقِينُ","tradPropre":"jusqu'à ce que nous vînt la vérité évidente [la mort]».","tradEn":"Until there came to us the certainty.\"","tradEs":"hasta que nos alcanzó la muerte [y con ella la certeza]\".","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>jusqu'à ce que la mort (l'évidence certaine) vienne les surprendre.</strong>","explicationEn":"47. We persisted in this denial until death came to us and prevented us from repenting.","explicationEs":"47. Persistimos en esta negación hasta que la muerte nos alcanzó, y ya no pudimos arrepentirnos”.","explicationAr":"وتمادينا في التكذيب به حتى جاءنا الموت، فحال بيننا وبين التوبة.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074047","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-46.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-48.html"},{"numVerset":48,"texteArabe":"فَمَا تَنفَعُهُمْ شَفَٰعَةُ الشَّٰفِعِينَ","tradPropre":"Ne leur profitera point donc, l'intercession des intercesseurs.","tradEn":"So there will not benefit them the intercession of [any] intercessors.","tradEs":"A estos no les beneficiará intercesión alguna.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le Jour de la Résurrection, l’intercession des anges, des prophètes et des pieux ne leur profitera pas, car l’une des conditions de l’acceptation de l’intercession est que le bénéficiaire de cette intercession soit agréé.","explicationEn":"48. On the Day of Judgment, the mediation of intercessors from the angels, prophets and pious ones, will not benefit them, because the requirement for the acceptance of intercession is that the thing for which intercession is made must be approved.","explicationEs":"48. En el Día del Juicio, la mediación de los intercesores de entre los ángeles, los profetas y los piadosos, no los beneficiará, porque el requisito para la aceptación de la intercesión es que el propósito por el cual se hace la intercesión debe ser aprobado por Allah.","explicationAr":"فما تنفعهم يوم القيامة وساطة الشافعين من الملائكة والنبيين والصالحين؛ لأن من شرط قَبول الشفاعة الرضا عن المشفوع له.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074048","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-47.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-49.html"},{"numVerset":49,"texteArabe":"فَمَا لَهُمْ عَنِ التَّذْكِرَةِ مُعْرِضِينَ","tradPropre":"Qu'ont-ils à se détourner du Rappel?","tradEn":"Then what is [the matter] with them that they are, from the reminder, turning away","tradEs":"¿Qué les pasa que se apartan de la amonestación [del Corán]","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pour quelle raison ces polythéistes se détournent-ils du Coran?","explicationEn":"49. What has made these idolaters turn away from the Qur’ān?!","explicationEs":"49. ¿Qué ha hecho que estos idólatras se alejen del Corán?","explicationAr":"أي شيء جعل هؤلاء المشركين معرضين عن القرآن؟!","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074049","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-48.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-50.html"},{"numVerset":50,"texteArabe":"كَأَنَّهُمْ حُمُرٞ مُّسْتَنفِرَةٞ","tradPropre":"Ils sont comme des onagres épouvantés,","tradEn":"As if they were alarmed donkeys","tradEs":"como si fueran cebras espantadas","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Comparaison des négateurs fuyant le Rappel à des ânes sauvages effarouchés,</strong>","explicationEn":"50. As if they, in their turning away from and aversion to it, are wild donkeys that are extremely resistant.","explicationEs":"50. En su alejamiento y aversión a él, ellos son como cebras espantadas.","explicationAr":"كأنهم في إعراضهم ونفورهم منه حُمُر وَحْش شديدة النفور.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074050","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-49.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-51.html"},{"numVerset":51,"texteArabe":"فَرَّتْ مِن قَسْوَرَةِ","tradPropre":"s'enfuyant devant un lion.","tradEn":"Fleeing from a lion?","tradEs":"huyendo de un león?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>qui s'enfuient à toute allure devant un lion (Qaswarah).</strong>","explicationEn":"51. That have fled from a lion out of fear for it.","explicationEs":"51. Que huyen de un león aterrorizadas.","explicationAr":"نفرت من أسد خوفًا منه.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074051","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-50.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-52.html"},{"numVerset":52,"texteArabe":"بَلْ يُرِيدُ كُلُّ امْرِيٕٖ مِّنْهُمْ أَن يُؤْتَىٰ صُحُفٗا مُّنَشَّرَةٗ","tradPropre":"Chacun d'eux voudrait plutôt qu'on lui apporte des feuilles tout étalées.","tradEn":"Rather, every person among them desires that he would be given scriptures spread about.","tradEs":"Ellos quisieran que descendieran [del cielo] páginas con un mensaje especial [que les confirmase que Mujámmad es un Mensajero de Dios].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Leur exigence orgueilleuse de recevoir chacun des manuscrits tout déployés venus du ciel,</strong>","explicationEn":"52. Instead, each one of these idolaters wants for there to be an open book by his head side that tells him that Muhammad is a messenger from Allah. The reason for this is not the lack of proof or weakness of evidence. It is only obstinacy and pride.","explicationEs":"52. Cada uno de estos idólatras pretende que haya un libro abierto a su lado que le diga que Mujámmad es un Mensajero de Allah. La razón por la que niegan el mensaje no es la falta de pruebas o la inconsistencia de las evidencias, solo es obstinación y soberbia.","explicationAr":"بل يريد كل واحد من هؤلاء المشركين أن يصبح عند رأسه كتاب منشور يخبره أن محمدًا رسول من الله، وليس سبب ذلك قلة البراهين أو ضعف الحجج، وإنما هو العناد والاستكبار.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074052","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-51.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-53.html"},{"numVerset":53,"texteArabe":"كَلَّا بَل لَّا يَخَافُونَ الْأٓخِرَةَ","tradPropre":"Ah! Non! C'est plutôt qu'ils ne craignent pas l'au-delà.","tradEn":"No! But they do not fear the Hereafter.","tradEs":"Pero no se lo concederemos, porque no tienen temor devocional a la vida del más allá.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Cela n’arrivera pas. La raison de leur égarement exagéré est qu’ils ne croient pas au châtiment de l’au-delà, demeurant de ce fait mécréants.","explicationEn":"53. The matter is not like that. In fact, the reason for their persistence in their misguidance is that they do not have faith in the punishment of the afterlife, so they remained in their disbelief.","explicationEs":"53. No les será concedido este libro que Allah bajó del cielo para ellos, porque la razón de su persistencia en su extravío es que no creen en el juicio de la otra vida, por lo que permanecen en su incredulidad.","explicationAr":"ليس الأمر كذلك، بل السبب في تماديهم في ضلالهم أنهم لا يؤمنون بعذاب الآخرة، فبقوا على كفرهم.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074053","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-52.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-54.html"},{"numVerset":54,"texteArabe":"كَلَّآ إِنَّهُ تَذْكِرَةٞ","tradPropre":"Ah! Non! Ceci est vraiment un Rappel.","tradEn":"No! Indeed, the Qur'an is a reminder","tradEs":"[El Corán] es una exhortación","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce Coran est une rappel et conseil bienveillant et un rappel.","explicationEn":"54. Indeed, this Qur’ān is an admonition and a reminder.","explicationEs":"54. Este Corán es una advertencia y una exhortación.","explicationAr":"ألا إن هذا القرآن موعظة وتذكير.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074054","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-53.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-55.html"},{"numVerset":55,"texteArabe":"فَمَن شَآءَ ذَكَرَهُ","tradPropre":"Quiconque veut, qu'il se le rappelle.","tradEn":"Then whoever wills will remember it.","tradEs":"para que reflexione quien quiera.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Quiconque veut lire le Coran et en tirer des enseignements, qu’il le lise et en tire des enseignements.","explicationEn":"55. Whoever wishes to read the Qur’ān and take lesson from it does so.","explicationEs":"55. Quien quiera leer el Corán y aprender de él que lo haga.","explicationAr":"فمن شاء أن يقرأ القرآن ويتعظ به قرأه واتعظ به.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074055","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-54.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-74-verset-56.html"},{"numVerset":56,"texteArabe":"وَمَا يَذْكُرُونَ إِلَّآ أَن يَشَآءَ اللَّهُ هُوَ أَهْلُ التَّقْوَىٰ وَأَهْلُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ","tradPropre":"Mais ils ne se rappelleront que si Allah veut. C'est Lui qui est Le plus digne d'être craint; et c'est Lui qui détient le pardon.","tradEn":"And they will not remember except that Allah wills. He is worthy of fear and adequate for [granting] forgiveness.","tradEs":"Pero solo lo harán aquellos para quienes Dios quiera la guía. Solo Él es digno de ser adorado, y solo Él es la fuente del perdón.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"<strong style='color:#ffffff;'>Conclusion rappelant que nul ne se souvient que par la Volonté d'Allāh, Seul digne d'être craint et Détenteur du pardon.</strong>","explicationEn":"56. None takes lesson from it besides those whom Allah wills to take lesson. He (may He be glorified) is worthy of being mindful of by the fulfilment of His instructions and the avoidance of His prohibitions. He is worthy of forgiving the sins of His servants when they repent to Him.","explicationEs":"56. Solo reflexionan sobre el Corán aquellos que Allah quiere que reflexionen. Allah es digno de que obedezcan Sus órdenes y se alejen de Sus prohibiciones. Allah perdona los pecados de Sus siervos cuando se arrepienten ante Él.","explicationAr":"وما يتعظون إلا أن يشاء الله أن يتعظوا، هو سبحانه أهل لأن يُتَّقَى بامتثال أوامره واجتناب نواهيه، وأهل لأن يغفر ذنوب عباده إذا تابوا إليه.","precisionConsensus":"","precisionEn":"","precisionEs":"","precisionAr":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"074056","lienPrecedent":"sourate-74-verset-55.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-75-verset-1.html"}]};